G5613.def:
ὡς, adverbial form of the relative pron. ὅς, ἥ, ὅ. 
__I. As relat. adv. of manner, as, like as, just as, even as; 
__1. with a demonstrative, like οὕτως, expressed or understood: οὕτως . . . ὡς, Marc 4:26, 1 Corinthiens 3:15, Éphésiens 5:28, Jacques 2:12, al.; ὡς . . . οὕτως, Actes 8:32, 1 Corinthiens 7:17, al.; elliptically (sc. οὕτως, οὕτω), with nom., Matthieu 6:29, al.; with accusative, Matthieu 19:19, Marc 12:31, al.; with prep., Matthieu 26:55, Marc 14:48, Luc 22:52, Jean 7:10, al.; with verb., Jean 15:6, 2 Corinthiens 3:1, Éphésiens 2:3, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:6, al.; with ptcp. (the ptcp. however not having the special force wh. it has in cl.; see Bl., §73, 5; 74, 6), Matthieu 7:29, Marc 1:22, Hébreux 13:17, al.; freq implying opinion or belief, Romains 9:32; so esp, with genitive absol., 1 Corinthiens 4:18, 2 Corinthiens 5:20, 1 Pierre 4:12, 2 Pierre 1:3. 
__2. Before numerals, about, nearly: Marc 5:13, Jean 1:40, Actes 5:7, al. 
__3. Before adjectives and adverbs, how: Romains 10:15 11:33, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:10; with superl., ὡς τάχιστα, as quickly as possible, Actes 17:15. 
__II. As conjunction; 
__1. temporal, 
__(a) as, when, since: Marc 9:21 14:72, Luc 1:23, Jean 2:9, al.; 
__(b) while, when, as long as: Luc 12:58, Jean 12:36, Galates 6:10 (Field, Notes, 191); ὡς ἄν (M, Pr., 167, and see: ἄν), Romains 15:24, 1 Corinthiens 11:34, Philippiens 2:23. 
__2. Final, in order that; with inf., in order to (M, Pr., 204n), Luc 9:52, Actes 20:24, Hébreux 7:9.
